      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That's twice the usual maximum for adults, which is 3,200 mg/day under physician supervision. Over-the-counter use is capped at 1,200 mg/day. A dose that high raises the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,600 mg/day total**, divided into a different schedule\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, tell me and include a note on the order about why. I can then enter it as written, though pharmacy will probably flag it. Otherwise, tell me the dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
